-- title:
--   Units of the first smooth local ring from vanishing orders
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an integer $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$; fix further modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing at the $q$-expansion pair), a witness `hKr` that the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ is $(X^{q}-Y)(X-Y^{q})$, witnesses `hα`, `hβ` that the two Hecke maps $\overline\alpha$, $\overline\beta$ at level $N$ and prime $q$ are integral ring homomorphisms, a place specialization $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Let $v$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$, the subfield of $k((q))$ generated by $j$ and $j_N$, and let $f$ be an element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ (Nq)$ which lies in the integers of the prolongation $R.R₁$ and whose $R₁$-residue is nonzero. Assume that $\mathrm{ord}_W f = 0$ for every place $W$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ (Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying $P.\mathrm{IsStrictFst}\ W$ (the geometric-level Frobenius sends $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ W$ to $P.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\ W$, while its square does not fix $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ W$) and $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ W = v$. Then both $f$ and $f^{-1}$ lie in $R.\mathrm{smoothLocalRingFst}\ v$, the intersection of the integers of $R.R₁$ with the valuation subrings of all such places $W$.
--
--   This says that an $R₁$-integral function with nonzero first residue and order zero at every first-kind strict place above $v$ is a unit of the local ring of the model at $v$ on the first branch; zeros and poles elsewhere are irrelevant. It is used in the verification that the tuple is a model, in the estimate `IsModel.neg_one_le_ord_residueFst_of_eq_one_add_mul_of_evalAt_ne`.
